# GoClaw — Go Best Practices

Sources: Uber Go Style Guide, Effective Go, JetBrains "10x Commandments of Go"

## Error handling

```go
// 1. Sentinel errors for known failure modes
var (
    ErrPermissionDenied = errors.New("permission denied")
    ErrToolNotFound     = errors.New("tool not found")
)

// 2. Always wrap with context
return fmt.Errorf("registry.Get %q: %w", name, ErrToolNotFound)

// 3. Match with errors.Is / errors.As
if errors.Is(err, ErrPermissionDenied) { ... }

// 4. Error strings: lowercase, no punctuation
// CORRECT:  "connection refused"
// WRONG:    "Connection refused."
```

## Interfaces

```go
// Keep interfaces small — 1 to 3 methods
type Tool interface {
    Name() string
    Execute(ctx context.Context, input string) (Result, error)
}

// Verify implementation at compile time
var _ Tool = (*ReadFileTool)(nil)
var _ llm.Client = (*OllamaClient)(nil)

// Accept interfaces, return concrete types
func NewRegistry() *Registry { ... }          // concrete return is fine
func Process(t Tool) error   { ... }          // accept interface
```

## Goroutines & channels

```go
// Always provide an exit path — no goroutine leaks
go func() {
    defer close(out)
    for {
        select {
        case out <- compute():
        case <-ctx.Done():
            return   // exit path
        }
    }
}()

// Explicit channel direction
func stream(ctx context.Context, out chan<- Event) { ... }
func consume(in <-chan Event) string { ... }

// Use sync.Mutex for shared state — not global vars
type Registry struct {
    mu    sync.Mutex
    items map[string]Tool
}
func (r *Registry) Get(name string) (Tool, bool) {
    r.mu.Lock()
    defer r.mu.Unlock()
    t, ok := r.items[name]
    return t, ok
}
```

## Testing patterns

```go
// Table-driven tests — always preferred
func TestPolicyEvaluate(t *testing.T) {
    cases := []struct {
        name string; mode Mode; want Decision
    }{
        {"allow", ModeAllow, DecisionAllow},
        {"deny",  ModeDeny,  DecisionDeny},
        {"ask",   ModeAsk,   DecisionAsk},
    }
    for _, tc := range cases {
        t.Run(tc.name, func(t *testing.T) {
            p := NewPolicy()
            p.Set("bash", tc.mode)
            if got := p.Evaluate("bash"); got != tc.want {
                t.Errorf("got %v, want %v", got, tc.want)
            }
        })
    }
}

// Use t.TempDir() — never os.TempDir() in tests
dir := t.TempDir()

// Mark helpers with t.Helper()
func requireNoError(t *testing.T, err error) {
    t.Helper()
    if err != nil { t.Fatalf("unexpected error: %v", err) }
}

// Run with race detector
// go test -race ./...
```

## Dependency injection

```go
// CORRECT — all dependencies explicit
func NewOrchestrator(cfg Config, client llm.Client, sess *session.Session) *Orchestrator {
    return &Orchestrator{cfg: cfg, llm: client, session: sess}
}

// WRONG — global mutable state
var defaultClient llm.Client
func init() { defaultClient = llm.NewOllama("") }
```

## Struct initialization

```go
// CORRECT — named fields always
p := permissions.Policy{
    global: ModeAsk,
}

// WRONG — positional
p := permissions.Policy{ModeAsk}
```

## Defer

```go
// Acquire → defer release immediately, before any error check on the resource
mu.Lock()
defer mu.Unlock()

resp, err := http.Get(url)
if err != nil { return err }
defer resp.Body.Close()
```

## Package design

```go
// Name the package after what it provides, not what it contains
package session   // not "sessionmanager"
package tools     // not "toolregistry"

// Avoid package-level init() — use explicit constructors
// WRONG:
func init() { globalRegistry.Register(&ReadFileTool{}) }

// CORRECT:
reg := tools.New()
reg.Register(&ReadFileTool{})
```

## Linting (run before every commit)

```bash
go vet ./...
staticcheck ./...       # go install honnef.co/go/tools/cmd/staticcheck@latest
go test -race ./...
```
